  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/DeadMoon0/TestFramework-Web",
  "published": "2026-08-15T21:38:36.067Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Initial release: REST API and SQL Server testing, model-derived schema, and stubbed dependencies.\nWorth knowing up front:\n- A status code is a result, not a failure. Api.Get(...) returns 404 immediately rather than retrying. Put Api.IsLive(...) in front of a call when a locally started host may still be warming up - that step, not the call, absorbs the startup 404/503.\n- Cookies are off by default. The HTTP clients are pooled per identifier, so a cookie jar would be shared by every run against that identifier; set ApiConfig.UseCookies only for an API whose session really is a cookie, and expect that session to be shared.\n- Stub.Reset(...) records a watermark by default instead of deleting the stub's request log, so it is safe against a stub shared with other runs. Only ClearServerLog deletes evidence, and only a stub this run owns gives fully isolated verification - narrow waits with WithHeader(...) on a shared one.\n- A SQL script is executed as one session, so #temp tables, SET options and a transaction opened in one GO batch survive into the next, as they do in SSMS.",
